Mara,

Apologies for the delay on this; I wanted to check the contract vehicles properly before answering. Answering your question of 16 February on the procurement path for the writing feedback tool:

1. This exceeds the informal quote threshold (policy PR-4.2), so we need an RFQ.

2. The cooperative contracts don't cover writing-feedback tools. I checked the three the System currently piggybacks on. Two are hardware and general software resale; the third covers learning management and proctoring but not AI writing feedback, and I am not comfortable stretching its scope.

3. The vendor demos and questionnaires you have run so far count as market research under the same policy, so nothing done to date needs to be repeated.

What I need from you: please send me the requirements section by Tuesday 9 March so I can issue the RFQ. Functional, technical, security and accessibility requirements, plus anything on support and data handling that you want to be scored rather than assumed. I will supply the boilerplate (terms, submission instructions, evaluation method). A draft in a Word document is fine; please don't send it as a slide deck.

Pricing must stay within the budget ceiling we discussed. Please do not quote it to the vendors, in the requirements or anywhere else.

Delphine, copying you as sponsor so you can see the route.

Regards,
Clement

Clement Oyelaran
Procurement Officer
System Procurement | Tarrow University System Office


